# Test: ze connect add + list round-trip through the live credential store
# VALIDATES: `ze connect add <host> --port --user` (password on stdin) hashes
#            the password and writes the credential to the live store
#            (connect.AddCredentials), and a subsequent `ze connect list`
#            reads it back and formats it as "<host>:<port> (user: <user>)"
#            (connect.ListRemotes). The add->list round-trip proves both the
#            write and read paths of the credential store offline.
# PREVENTS: regressions where connect stops persisting credentials or where
#           list stops reading/formatting them.
# SCOPE: the parse runner exposes only the FINAL command's stdout to
#   expect=stdout, so each per-subcommand assertion must end on the subcommand
#   under test. add and list are covered here via the round-trip; remove is
#   covered in cli-connect-remove.ci.
# HARNESS NOTE: the asserted line comes from the closing `connect list`; the
# add step is verified transitively (an empty store would make list print
# "no remotes configured" and fail this assertion).
# ISOLATION: ze.config.dir=. selects the per-test working directory.
# SEED: init creates the tree before offline credential writes.
stdin=init:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
secret
127.0.0.1
2222
test-connect
EOF_INIT
tmpfs=placeholder.conf:terminator=EOF_PH
system {
	host seedhost
}
EOF_PH

stdin=pw:terminator=EOF_PW
secretpw
EOF_PW

option=env:var=ze.config.dir:value=.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze connect add 10.0.1.5 --port 2223 --user admin:stdin=pw:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze connect list:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=10.0.1.5:2223 (user: admin)
